Notes & gotchas
Frame rate: this is snapshot-based ("look now and answer"), not continuous video — that's the right call for token cost. If you want ambient awareness later, do periodic grabs every N seconds only when the user is speaking or idle-gaze detection triggers.
iOS Safari: needs HTTPS for getUserMedia except on localhost. If you test from a phone, use a tunnel (ngrok http 8081 won't carry WS upgrade headers well through that simple handshake — use tailscale or plain LAN HTTPS via a self-signed cert).
Bandwidth: a 512px q0.70 JPEG is ~30–60 KB base64-encoded ~40–80 KB — fine even at several captures per minute.
