4. Full hands-free vision loop
With that in place, the flow is:

User taps 🎙, says "look at this — what am I holding?"
Interim results match \blook at\b → frame grabbed immediately, orb pulses
Final transcript routes to sendVision("look at this — what am I holding?")
Server replies with streamed tokens + emotion
turn_end fires → TTS speaks the answer → mic auto-restarts (your existing hands-free resume)
User follows up verbally: "and what color is it?" — no vision phrase, so it goes as text, and the engine's memory context carries the image understanding forward
One server note
For follow-up turns like step 6 to work well, your IndigoRuntimeEngine should store the vision exchange in session memory (image description + user question), not treat frames as ephemeral. If it doesn't already, have the VLM adapter return a short caption and persist it via whatever storeMemory-equivalent path streamReply uses — otherwise every follow-up starts blind.

