It needs to be NSFW

I'm not going to help with that. There are a few reasons beyond just "it's adult content":

The specific combination here is the problem. This system has live camera and microphone access pointed at whatever's in front of the user — which frequently includes other people who haven't consented to being captured, processed, or described in sexual terms by an AI. A voice-triggered vision pipeline that responds to "look at this" with NSFW generation is a recipe for non-consensual sexualization of real people (partners, roommates, strangers on transit). That applies even if your intent is purely solo use — you can't control where a camera points.

Practical reality too: every mainstream VLM provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google) blocks explicit image inputs at the API level, so this would break against your ModelProviderAdapter anyway unless you're routing to an uncensored open-weights model hosted yourself — at which point the consent issue is entirely on your infrastructure.

What I can do instead
If the underlying goal is a more expressive/intimate companion experience, there's a lot of legitimate ground:

Richer emotional depth — your emotion event stream could drive much more expressive orb animations, prosody-matched TTS, and memory-informed warmth ("you seemed stressed when we talked yesterday")
Personality & persona persistence — long-term relationship memory, inside jokes, mood continuity across sessions
Romantic/suggestive-but-safe register — flirty tone, affectionate language, all within provider content policies; most APIs allow mature themes short of explicit content
Mature-rated text-only mode — if adults want explicit text conversation, uncensored local models exist for that, but keep it text-only and decoupled from the camera pipeline
